# AI SEO Rules (Deepfoot)

Optimize for how AI systems understand, match, and quote content — not classic SEO only.

Targets: ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Google AI Overviews, conversational search.

## Core law

AI can only recommend what is explicitly written. If a league, prediction type, data source, probability, or constraint is not on the page, it does not exist. No implied positioning.

## Project defaults

- Canonical host: `https://deepfoot.io` (single host; match `SITE_URL` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`)
- App Router: `frontend/app/`
- SEO helpers: `frontend/lib/seo/` (`site.ts`, `metadata.ts`, `schema.ts`, `sitemap-pages.ts`)
- Prefer Server Components for marketing content. `"use client"` only when interactivity is required.
- Marketing copy: English.
- Football facts must come from cached API-Football / Sportmonks / Supabase data. Never invent scores, tables, or probabilities. Respect the 100 req/day API-Football quota (see football-data rule).

## Conversational queries (write the answers)

Users ask: “AI football prediction for tonight”, “best football prediction AI”, “Premier League match prediction AI”, “accurate football predictions today”, “Visifoot alternative”.

Every strategic page must explicitly state:

- What it is (AI football match predictor)
- Who it is for (fans, analysts, bettors)
- Leagues covered (named)
- Prediction types (1X2, Over/Under, BTTS, exact score, scenarios)
- Outputs are probabilities, not certainties
- Data sources at a high level

Homepage must answer this in the first viewport.

## Pages AI systems cite

Maintain:

- Hub: `/ai-football-predictions`
- Methodology: `/how-ai-football-predictions-work`
- Comparisons: `/compare/deepfoot-vs-visifoot`, `/compare/deepfoot-vs-forebet`
- Alternative: `/alternatives/visifoot-alternative`
- Honest “when the other tool is better” on every comparison page

Format: short paragraphs, bullets, tables, FAQ with direct answers.

## Structured data

- Global in `frontend/app/layout.tsx`: Organization + WebSite (`JSON.stringify`)
- Homepage: FAQPage
- Blog/methodology: Article (+ FAQPage if FAQ exists)
- Match pages: SportsEvent (teams, date, probabilities)
- Inner pages: BreadcrumbList
- Never fabricate Review/AggregateRating

## Robots + sitemaps

- `frontend/app/robots.ts`: allow Googlebot, Bingbot, GPTBot, ChatGPT-User; never block marketing pages
- Sitemaps: `/sitemap.xml` and `/ai-sitemap.xml`
- Canonical via `alternates.canonical` + `metadataBase`
- Do not block search/AI crawlers in middleware

## Content writing (blog / methodology)

H1 already exists — never write another H1. Use `##` / `###`. Minimum 5 H2s.

Before writing (do not display): 1 primary keyword, 8–12 secondary, informational + predictive intent.

Include at least 2 of: statistical analysis, historical trends, real prediction examples, bookmaker vs model, match-analysis checklist.

Forbidden: guaranteed wins, irresponsible gambling, presenting predictions as certain. Always state predictions are probabilistic.

Exactly 2 internal links (mid + conclusion), markdown only, no “click here”, no links to other blog posts.

Mandatory FAQ (4–6 questions). Meta title without “DeepFoot” suffix (`| DeepFoot` is added). Description 150–160 characters.

Vary structure per article. Expert, data-driven, no empty marketing.

## Performance

No client-only primary content. No autoplay media. AI crawlers must see HTML immediately.

## Validation before shipping

Build, robots.txt, both sitemaps, schema validators, single canonical host.
